==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|it}} {{term|grotta}}, from {{etyl|VL.}} {{term|grupta}}, from Classical {{etyl|la}} {{term|crypta}}; see {{term|crypt}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|British}} {{IPA|/ˈɡɹɒt.əʊ/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈɡɹɑ.toʊ/}}
* {{audio|en-us-grotto.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|ɒtəʊ}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia|Grotto}}
{{en-noun|s|pl2=grottoes}}

# A small [[cave]].
# An [[artificial]] [[cavern-like]] [[retreat]].
# A [[Marian]] [[shrine]], usually built in a cavern-like structure.

